==English==
[[File:Alphabet soup, empty.jpg|thumb|A nearly empty bowl of alphabet soup ''(sense 1)'' with noodles spelling out “{{smc|the end}}” on the side]]

===Noun===
{{en-noun|~}}

# {{senseid|en|soup with letter-shaped noodles}} A type of [[soup]] that contains [[noodle]]s in the shape of various [[alphabetical]] [[letter]]s, sometimes also [[number]]s.
#: {{mer|en|alfabeto}}
#: {{ux|en|Parents have been entertaining their children at mealtime with '''alphabet soup''' since the nineteenth century.}}
# {{senseid|en|cryptic communication}} {{lb|en|figuratively}} An [[overabundance]] of [[acronym]]s and [[abbreviation]]s, which may appear [[cryptic]] to [[noninitiate]]s.
#: {{ux|en|The various engineering teams' correspondence on circuit board design was an '''alphabet soup''' to outsiders.}}
#* {{quote-text|en|year=2006|author=Amy L. Stone|title=More than adding a T: transgender inclusion in Michigan gay rights ordinances, 1992-2000
|passage=And particularly in headlines and written materials, gay was used over LGBT. One ambivalent heterosexual ally explained this decision-making: I think there were several people who were sensitive to issues like that about do we use the word lesbian? Do we use the word transgender? And it's not that we didn't use those words, but in general, if you're doing a brochure and you have a headline, you don't include the whole '''alphabet soup'''.}}
# {{senseid|en|people or organizations labeled}} {{lb|en|figuratively|metonymically}} A [[quantity]] of [[people]] or [[organization]]s that are referred to by [[acronym]]s.
#: {{cot|en|alphabet agency|alt1=alphabet agencies}}
#: {{ux|en|too many three-letter agencies, constituting an '''alphabet soup'''}}

